---
import ToolLayout from '../../layouts/ToolLayout.astro';
import CodeToPrompt from '../../components/CodeToPrompt.jsx';
---

<ToolLayout
  title="Code Snippet to Prompt Converter"
  description="Paste code and instantly get a well-formed prompt for explaining, debugging, optimizing, documenting, or converting it."
>
  <CodeToPrompt client:load slot="tool" />

  <h2>Stop retyping the same prompt scaffolding</h2>
  <p>
    Asking an AI model about code usually means the same repetitive
    wrapper text — "explain this", "find bugs in this" — around a code
    block. This tool handles the wrapper so you can focus on the code
    itself.
  </p>

  <h2>How to use this</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Paste your code and set the language.</li>
    <li>Pick a task — explain, debug, optimize, document, or convert.</li>
    <li>Copy the formatted prompt into your AI tool of choice.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>FAQ</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>Does this send my code anywhere?</strong> No — the prompt is
    built entirely in your browser. You choose where to paste and send it.
  </p>
</ToolLayout>
